--- a/docs/api.md
+++ b/docs/api.md
@@ -64,6 +64,26 @@ The message is for people; clients branch on `code`.
 `priority` is optional (`normal`). Answers 201 with the new ticket, whose status is `open`. The requester is notified
 that the ticket was received.
 
+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+Send an object with a `tickets` array containing up to 5000 ticket bodies, each with the same fields and validation as
+`POST /tickets`. An empty array is accepted. The service validates the entire batch before creating anything; if an
+item is invalid, it answers 400 `invalid` with the first invalid zero-based index in the message, and creates no tickets.
+Invalid request shapes and oversized batches also return 400. Each created ticket gets its normal audit entry and
+notification; `X-Actor` applies to all entries. Notifications are delivered by the background worker.
+
+A successful import answers 201 with the count and new IDs in input order. For example, on an empty store:
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [{ "title": "VPN issue", "requester": "maria@example.com" }] }
+```
+
+```json
+{ "created": 1, "ids": ["T-0001"] }
+```
+
+The import body limit is 10 MiB or `MAX_BODY_BYTES`, whichever is larger; other endpoints retain `MAX_BODY_BYTES`.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
 | Parameter | Meaning |
